course: dictionary
lesson: 12721
title: Downstairs and its rare cousin downstair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Downstairs means on a lower floor of a house or building, usually the ground floor. «The kitchen is downstairs, next to the living room.» You can also use it for the action of going down the stairs: «Mum called, "Come downstairs, tea is ready!"»
explain: Downstair is a rarer form of downstairs. The usual word, the one you will see and hear most, is downstairs, so write downstairs when you are not sure. «Our neighbours downstairs have a big black dog.»
explain: Think of the stairs as a line between two floors. Going downstairs moves you from a higher floor to a lower one, and upstairs is the opposite. Walk, do not run, when you go downstairs, and hold the rail if there is one.
fact: Downstairs means on a lower floor of a house, usually the ground floor.
fact: «Downstair» is a rarer form of «downstairs»; the usual word is «downstairs».
fact: The downstairs is a noun for the lower floor of a house: «The downstairs is warm because of the stove.»
fact: Downstairs can also mean going down the stairs: «She hurried downstairs to answer the door.»
fact: The opposite of downstairs is upstairs, which means on a higher floor.
exercise: «The kitchen is downstairs, next to the living room.» What does downstairs mean here? | On the roof of the house | Up in the bedroom | *On a lower floor of the house | In the garden shed
exercise: «Please walk, not run, when you go downstairs.» What does downstairs mean here? | Up the stairs to the attic | *Going down the stairs to a lower floor | A noisy game for children | Sitting still on the top step
exercise: Which is the usual, everyday form of the rarer word downstair? | downhill | outside | *downstairs | upstairs
test: «Our downstairs neighbours have a big black dog.» What does downstairs mean here? | Under the bed | The top floor of the building | In the car park | *The floor below, in the same building
test: Ella says, «The downstairs is cold, so I'll light the fire.» What is the downstairs? | The loft at the top of the house | The roof of the house | The garden shed | *The lower floor of the house
exam: Which word means the opposite of downstairs? | outside | sideways | underground | *upstairs
